 "note": "A Roundabout 6 hub with a switch on each side of it (half-turn symmetry). Each switch either carries the main road (hub <-> home, s1) or swings across to join the two hub spokes beside it (s2), closing the ring round the hub and cutting the home off the axis. Homes keep two outer roads. (Rulebook pass 2026-10-28: the rotors became switches - a rigid rotor cannot turn between a 180-degree main road and the spokes' 100 degrees; the hub's four spoke platforms survive the Last Stand.)",
 "geometricSymmetry": true,
 "labVariant": {
  "junctions": true
 },
 "experimental": true,
 "ruleWaivers": {
  "N13": "rotor -> switch (rulebook pass 2026-10-28): the two states join decks of different tiers / spacing, which N13 forbids for a rigid rotor; the connections per state are the original's"
 },
